{
    "about": "Groups 1d, Core 6: the settings document opened by the ledger itself and a family folder opened from route 25 (self-grant first, else the area grant). Both twins build each case over the roster-call family (tests/common/roster_calls.rs, roster-calls-testkit.ts) through their own code (the core's AreaLedger::use_settings_envelope and open_family_area; the worker's settingsKeyOpen/settingsOpen and groupOpenArea), check `expected`, write what they sealed into their roster-call document, and read the other twin's to the same outcomes (tests/common/settings_areas.rs, settings-areas-testkit.ts). Settings cases are person 1's device: `steps` are settings reads in order (`document` as below, `envelope` v2 unless legacy, none or version-3, `key` own unless other-root or missing, `tamper` flips a ciphertext byte), then acceptance of the family's history, and when accepted, person 4's admission and person 2's join code. A document is version 2 with every other person's version 3 pin and the family's pin at the head unless it says otherwise: `contacts` a list of [key, value] (key p2..p5, P4 for p4 in capitals; value {pin: whose keys, userId, without: [fields], with: {field: value}} or {raw: any}) or {raw: any}; `groups` {raw: the family's value} or {rawGroups: the whole member}. Area cases are person 2's device opening A1, A2 (deleted), A3 (key 2 since roster 7) or a foreign id: `grant` person 1's grant of [area index, key version] at `version` (`granterKey` false when route 6 serves no identity for them), `selfGrant` person 2's own of `key` at `version` for `area` under `group` (family or other) and `root` (own or other), `envelopeVersion` to damage it.",
